# Current theses

## Thesis T-static-site-deployment: Publish only the verified static allowlist
Status: accepted
Based-on: user:2026-09-17 site deployment plan

### Guidance
Treat this folder as the only authored source for openhint.dev. Package public
files through the repository allowlist. Before production writes, confirm that
the configured target serves the live domain, require strict host-key checks,
and back up every managed target. After SCP, remove only inventoried legacy
HINT paths; never delete unknown hosting content or rules.

### Rationale
SCP adds and overwrites but does not remove obsolete pages, while a broad
delete can damage unrelated hosting state. Verified targeting, bounded backup,
and an exact cleanup manifest make the non-atomic deployment recoverable.

### Revisit when
The hosting provider offers an atomic release mechanism or the document root
becomes exclusive to HINT with a separately verified retention policy.

